<title>USA: Omaha hogs off $1.50/2.50 - USDA.</title>
<headline>Omaha hogs off $1.50/2.50 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Barrows and gilts were $1.50 to mostly 42.50 lower. Top $53.50 per cwt. - USDA</p>
<p>US 1-3    220-260 lbs    52.50-53.50, mostly 52.50</p>
<p>US 2-3    260-280 lbs    51.50-52.00</p>
<p>Sows: 25 percent. Steady. Top 53.00.</p>
<p>US 1-3    350-450 lbs    44.00 to mostly 44.50</p>
<p>	    450-500 lbs    49.00</p>
<p>US 2-3    500-700 lbs    52.00-53.00</p>
<p>Hogs:  800	 Sltr - 800     Fdrs - None</p>
</text>
